{
  "about": "madar_inventory::purchase — hand-computed. Quantities are read as the decimal they print as and rounded to 3 dp half away from zero, as the numeric(12,3) column stores them (quantity_dec; milli is the same grain in thousandths). line_costs and delivery_cost are MadarRust purchasing/handlers.rs's, branch for branch, with that rounding fixed (D7: the backend rounded 0.0625 half to even, to 0.062). Decimals are strings; a unit cost is 8 dp, a line total whole piastres (half away from zero). estimate_line_total = cost per stock unit × qty × (purchase unit factor / stock unit factor), exact, rounded once. An error is the server's message.",
